{title: Praise to the Lord, the Almighty}
{artist: Joachim Neander / Catherine Winkworth (trans.)}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: F}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{score: praise-to-the-lord-the-almighty.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Praise to the Lord, the Al[D]mighty, the [G]King of cre[C]ation
O my [G]soul, praise Him, for [D]He is thy [G]health and sal[D]vation
All ye who [G]hear
Now to His [C]temple draw [G]near
Join me in [D]glad ado[G]ration
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Praise to the Lord, who o'er [D]all things so [G]wondrously [C]reigneth
Shelters thee [G]under His wings, yea, so [D]gently sus[G]tain[D]eth
Hast thou not [G]seen
How thy de[C]sires e'er have [G]been
Granted in [D]what He or[G]daineth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Praise to the Lord, who doth [D]prosper thy [G]work and de[C]fend thee
Surely His [G]goodness and mercy here [D]daily at[G]tend [D]thee
Ponder a[G]new
What the Al[C]mighty can [G]do
If with His [D]love He be[G]friend thee
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Praise to the Lord! O let [D]all that is [G]in me a[C]dore Him
All that hath [G]life and breath, come [D]now with [G]praises be[D]fore Him
Let the A[G]men
Sound from His [C]people a[G]gain
Gladly for [D]aye we a[G]dore Him
{end_of_verse}
